<title>BELGIUM: EU experts to study rising sugar output estimates.</title>
<headline>EU experts to study rising sugar output estimates.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's sugar management committee will on Wednesday discuss rising sugar production estimates, an EU official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The balance sheet is on the agenda and it will be the first occasion when the estimates can be assessed based on early crop liftings and the indications are that the figures are improving,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Trade sources told Reuters that the latest unofficial estimates put the EU 15 production forecast &quot;significantly up&quot; from the last national beet test estimates at the end of September.</p>
<p>The total beet sugar estimate for 1996/97 at the end of September was 15.417 million tonnes compared with 15.636 in 1995/96.</p>
<p>In addition to deciding on the usual weekly tenders and molasses duties the committee is scheduled to hold an ongoing discussion on the coefficients used to calculate the sugar content of processed products.</p>
</text>
